## Work Log — 2026-09-22

> 09:34 am – 03:39 pm · +1137 / -124 lines · `audit-lite` (fix/submission-cancelled-request-terminal)

### Summary
The day went to the report submission flow in `audit-lite`. Two small UX fixes merged: #2037 fixes the waiting-state logic and #2039 fixes the delivered-report wording and toast position. Most of the day was on #2040. It makes report-sync retry submissions that never reached the server, fixes how dropped signatures are handled, and adds a batch of submission-screen fixes, including a dedicated screen for server rejections. A flight-recorder log from a field device drove several of those fixes, starting with the wrong "files still to send" count.

### Tasks & Changes

#### Submission waiting state uses the device's own offline status
- **Repo:** `audit-lite` · branch: `fix/submission-cancelled-request-terminal`
- **What was done:** The submission screen's waiting state now uses the device's own offline status to decide what to show. Merged first thing in the morning.
- **Commits:**
  - `c8b1238d` — fix: read the device's own offline verdict for the waiting state (#2037)
- **PR:** [#2037 — fix: read the device's own offline verdict for the submission screen's waiting state](https://github.com/Nimbly-Technologies/audit-lite/pull/2037)

#### Delivered-report wording and toast position
- **Repo:** `audit-lite` · branch: `fix/submission-cancelled-request-terminal`
- **What was done:** Rewrote the delivered-report message to open with the success. The old line ended on "no longer on this device", which users read as the report being deleted. Also moved the toast. Built on `fix/submission-toast-copy-and-position` and merged after the review comments were addressed. Updated the repo docs and the ADR in Notion to match.
- **Commits:**
  - `d9a6b821` — fix(submission): delivered-report copy and toast position (#2039)
- **PR:** [#2039 — fix(submission): delivered-report copy and toast position](https://github.com/Nimbly-Technologies/audit-lite/pull/2039)

#### Report-sync: retry submissions that never reached the server
- **Repo:** `audit-lite` · branch: `fix/submission-cancelled-request-terminal`
- **What was done:** A submission whose request was cancelled before it reached the server used to be treated as final. The drain now retries it. Also fixed how dropped signature slots are handled: their path key is now left out entirely instead of being set to an empty value, and the drain's attachment pre-check skips them so they don't block the upload.
- **Commits:**
  - `beeb47aa` — fix(report-sync): retry a submission whose request never reached the server
  - `2525dc9f` — fix(report-sync): keep a dropped signature's path key absent, not empty
  - `c448876f` — fix(report-sync): skip dropped signature slots in the drain's attachment prevalidation
- **PR:** [#2040 — fix(report-sync): retry a submission whose request never reached the server](https://github.com/Nimbly-Technologies/audit-lite/pull/2040)

#### Submission screen fixes and a dedicated rejection screen
- **Repo:** `audit-lite` · branch: `fix/submission-cancelled-request-terminal`
- **What was done:**
  - **Diagnosis:** A flight-recorder log from a OnePlus CPH2487 on Android 16 showed "0 file(s) still need sending" while 19 attachments were still queued, and the retake/retry sections never appeared.
  - **Fixes from that:** The count now tracks attachments still to send instead of failed uploads, and the screen waits for the upload rows to load before settling on a state.
  - **Other screen fixes:** Timestamps now show the date and time zone. The back button has a destination. The force-submit dialog's buttons are stacked. The stopped card no longer says the report is "editable again".
  - **Rejection screen:** A server rejection now gets its own screen with "Reopen" and "Submit again" actions.
- **Commits:**
  - `5e877398` — fix(submission): stack the force-submit dialog's buttons
