## Work Log — 2026-09-29

> 11:08 am – 04:56 pm · +1652 / -240 lines · `audit-lite` (fix/auth-park-attachment-upload)

### Summary
Shipped two reliability fixes in `audit-lite`'s upload and submission path. The first stops an expired session from writing off an attachment; the app now parks the upload until re-auth (PR #2064). The second, PR #2065, fixes four bugs: a dead question row, a report delivered with attachment keys that had no bytes behind them, a needless Retake after the app was killed mid-upload, and the delivering submit going unrecorded. PR #2065 is merged to master. Later in the day I looked into a new submission report from Discord, checked the trend on a production Sentry issue, and set up Bitwarden autofill for test accounts.

### Tasks & Changes

#### Park expired sessions instead of writing off attachments
- **Repo:** `audit-lite` · branch: `fix/auth-park-attachment-upload`
- **What was done:** When the auth token has expired, an attachment upload is now parked instead of being marked failed for good. It recovers once the user logs in again. The chosen approach adds a new outcome tag and accepts a short recovery delay (up to about 60s after re-auth) rather than widening `isBlocked`, which would have changed the notification copy too. The docs were updated before the code changes. A follow-up narrowed the park so it only applies to refusals that a new token actually fixes. Master, which now includes #2065, was merged back into the branch. Progress was posted on Fizzy card 1774.
- **Commits:**
  - `f5d4a665` — fix: park an expired session instead of writing the attachment off
  - `a70f4d4d` — Merge branch 'master' into fix/auth-park-attachment-upload
  - `4d16b0f4` — fix: keep the session park to the refusals a new token actually fixes
- **PR:** [#2064 — fix: park an expired session instead of writing the attachment off (#1774)](https://github.com/Nimbly-Technologies/audit-lite/pull/2064)

#### Outbox submission fixes
- **Repo:** `audit-lite` · branch: `fix/auth-park-attachment-upload` (built on `fix/outbox-submission-bugs`, pushed 12:51–16:06, then merged to master)
- **What was done:** Fixed four bugs in the submission path:
  - a question row that stopped responding;
  - a report delivered with five attachment keys that had no uploaded bytes behind them;
  - a Retake prompt shown for no reason after the app was killed mid-upload;
  - the submit that delivered the report not being recorded.
- **Commits:**
  - `b0ccf600` — fix(submission): a dead question row, a report delivered with five attachment keys that had no bytes behind them, a needless Retake after the app was killed mid-upload, and the submit that delivered it going unrecorded (#2065)
- **PR:** [#2065 — fix(submission): a dead question row, a report delivered with five attachment keys that had no bytes behind them, a needless Retake after the app was killed mid-upload, and the submit that delivered it going unrecorded](https://github.com/Nimbly-Technologies/audit-lite/pull/2065)

### Meetings
- **Stability Stand-up** — 02:00 PM–02:15 PM (15 min)

### Investigation & Research

#### Submission stuck at 54/54 (Discord report)
- **Repo:** `audit-lite`
- **Question:** Why did a user's submission reach 54/54 with nothing left to repair and then stop? I pulled the attachments, the flight recorder logs and the Sentry events for those submission attempts.
- **Outcome:** Reaching 54/54 turned out to be a known, documented carve-out, not a stale message as I first thought. The core defect is that `derive-submission-state.ts` has two definitions of "uploaded" that disagree. The proposed fix is to use one definition of "uploaded" across both call sites. The logs didn't show why the submission itself stopped (Bug 2), so that is still unknown.
- **Time:** ~16:36–16:58

#### Sentry issue 7735846489 trend
- **Repo:** `audit-lite`
- **Question:** What does production Sentry issue [7735846489](https://nimbly-technologies.sentry.io/issues/7735846489/) mean, is it declining, and how many users are still on 2.16.x?
- **Outcome:** Worked out what causes the error, checked whether it is declining, and counted how many users are still on 2.16.x, to judge whether it will fade out as people upgrade.
- **Time:** 12:54–13:02

#### Bitwarden autofill for test accounts
- **Repo:** `audit-lite`
- **Question:** How can Bitwarden on my phone, backed by the office's self-hosted Vaultwarden, autofill test-account logins in the Nimbly Lite app?
- **Outcome:** Add `androidapp://com.sustainnovationgroup.nimblylite` as a URI on each test login in Bitwarden. I then tried to set this up on the connected device over adb.
- **Time:** 16:50–16:59

### Notes
- **PR #2064** is still open. It now carries the merge from master and the follow-up that narrows the park.
- **54/54 submission bug:** next step is the single-definition fix in `derive-submission-state.ts` in a new PR. Why the submission stopped (Bug 2) is still unknown.
- Andi Muhamad Primabudi was on leave.
